State management is the process of controlling, 
updating, and sharing data (state) in an application so 
that the UI always reflects the latest data correctly.
USING BLOC AND EQUATABLE
“BLOC is a state management pattern for Flutter that 
enforces separation between UI and business logic via 
events and states. The UI dispatches events, the Bloc 
runs logic and emits states, and the UI reacts. It’s great 
for testability, predictability and scaling large apps; 
use Cubit when you want a lighter-weight option.”
THE MAIN ELEMENTS BLOC=>
1.Build When : BuildWhen takes the previous bloc 
state and current bloc state and returns a boolean.
If buildWhen returns true, builder will be called with 
state and the widget will rebuild.
If buildWhen returns false, builder will not be called 
with state and no rebuild will occur. 
2.BlocBuilder: for rebuilding UI on state change 
Rebuilds a widget in response to new states emitted by 
Bloc/Cubit. 3.BocListener – for one-time side effects
 Purpose> Listens to Bloc state changes but does 
not rebuild UI. >Used for side effects like: , Navigation 
,Showing a SnackBar Showing Dialog ,4. BlocConsumer
– combines BlocBuilder + BlocListener Purpose: A 
shortcut to use both UI rebuild (BlocBuilder) and side 
effects (BlocListener) together.Has both a listener and 
builder. 5. BlocProvide 6. Bloc Repository